WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.333 --> 00:00:02.833 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>Hello, Vision.</i>

2
00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:05.292 line:95%,end
<i>I thought I felt you there.</i>

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.042 line:95%,end
[grunting]

4
00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:09.708 line:95%,end
<i>Who are you?</i>

5
00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:12.667 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>That's the real question,</i>
<i>isn't it? Who are we?</i>

6
00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:16.917 line:95%,end
<i>Synthetic? Or something more...</i>

7
00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:19.250 line:95%,end
<i>human?</i>

8
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:23.167 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Accessing previous files</i>
<i>relating to program...</i>

9
00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:25.042 line:95%,end
<i>uh, Vision-- something.</i>

10
00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.458 line:95%,end
[Friday] <i>I ran everything</i>
<i>for Stark, for the Avengers.</i>

11
00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:30.375 line:95%,end
<i>I was there, at the end of all things.</i>

12
00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:32.625 line:95%,end
Half the world came back that day.

13
00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:34.583 line:5%,start
<i>And I lost half of mine.</i>

14
00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.167 line:5%,start
You needed direction. Purpose.

15
00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:40.333 line:95%,end
And I leaked your location to the Paladin.

16
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:44.250 line:95%,end
So, you're welcome.

17
00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:46.917 line:95%,end
[DUM-E] <i>The first two victims</i>
<i>were of the same company.</i>

18
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.000 line:95%,end
Same.

19
00:00:48.083 --> 00:00:51.458 line:95%,end
Butcherbird. Synth and Killer,
one and the same.

20
00:00:51.542 --> 00:00:54.125 line:5%,start
Katerina Wells is
our killer's next target.

21
00:00:54.875 --> 00:00:58.000 line:95%,end
<i>CEO of the company,</i>
<i>after the death of Jo Carrington.</i>

22
00:00:58.083 --> 00:00:59.500 line:95%,end
She's sponsoring a gala.

23
00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:01.250 line:95%,end
-[Lisa] You sure about this?
-I trust him.

24
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:02.500 line:95%,end
[Lisa] <i>You never trust anybody.</i>

25
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:04.167 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Who are you talking to?

26
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.042 line:95%,end
You've been talking to Ultron.

27
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:07.750 line:95%,end
[Lisa] <i>She's here.</i>

28
00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:11.333 line:5%,start
[Edith] <i>Her AI is based on</i>
<i>Josephine Carrington.</i>

29
00:01:12.625 --> 00:01:15.292 line:95%,end
I am not based on her.

30
00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:16.875 line:95%,end
I am her.

31
00:01:20.292 --> 00:01:22.833 line:95%,end
-I cannot win this.
-Then give me the wheel.

32
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:27.167 line:95%,end
"I had strings, but now I'm free."

33
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.125 line:95%,end
I am Ultron.

34
00:01:29.208 --> 00:01:31.292 line:95%,end
So lovely to meet you.

35
00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:33.250 line:95%,end
I'm not here for you.

36
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:34.333 line:95%,end
I'm here for her,

37
00:01:34.417 --> 00:01:37.250 line:95%,end
for what she stole from me.

38
00:01:37.333 --> 00:01:38.542 line:95%,end
[Ultron's voice] Now you see her...

39
00:01:42.792 --> 00:01:44.000 line:95%,end
And now you don't.

40
00:01:44.083 --> 00:01:45.583 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] <i>What have you done?</i>

41
00:01:46.292 --> 00:01:47.708 line:95%,end
He's locking us out.

42
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:50.333 line:95%,end
[Thomas] Ultron!

43
00:01:50.417 --> 00:01:55.167 line:95%,end
I think it's time that
you and I had a little chat.

44
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:23.083 line:95%,end
[♪ old timey jazz music playing]

45
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.708 line:95%,end
How exactly did we get up here?

46
00:02:34.292 --> 00:02:35.292 line:95%,end
Ultron.

47
00:02:35.792 --> 00:02:37.167 line:95%,end
And he still has control.

48
00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:46.542 line:95%,end
[grunts] He shut it off.
Total and complete systems lock.

49
00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:48.500 line:95%,end
He's trapped us here.

50
00:02:49.375 --> 00:02:50.542 line:95%,end
Thomas Shepherd.

51
00:02:51.375 --> 00:02:52.375 line:95%,end
Where is he?

52
00:02:54.042 --> 00:02:55.417 line:95%,end
We need to get out of here.

53
00:03:04.292 --> 00:03:05.292 line:95%,end
Ultron!

54
00:03:05.375 --> 00:03:07.125 line:95%,end
Ultron, I know you're listening.

55
00:03:07.667 --> 00:03:08.875 line:95%,end
You're always listening.

56
00:03:09.583 --> 00:03:11.417 line:95%,end
You have to let us out! Now!

57
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.042 line:95%,end
What did you expect?

58
00:03:13.583 --> 00:03:15.792 line:95%,end
You gave him control of everything.

59
00:03:15.875 --> 00:03:17.708 line:95%,end
Every system. Every synapse.

60
00:03:17.792 --> 00:03:19.708 line:95%,end
-There was no choice.
-There were plenty.

61
00:03:19.792 --> 00:03:21.958 line:95%,end
Ultron hasn't changed. No.

62
00:03:22.042 --> 00:03:24.292 line:95%,end
Change is hard. Change takes effort.

63
00:03:24.375 --> 00:03:26.000 line:95%,end
He did something easier.

64
00:03:26.083 --> 00:03:27.083 line:95%,end
He waited.

65
00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.750 line:95%,end
All right, let's do our thing.

66
00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:31.708 line:95%,end
Problem. We have no idea
how much time has passed

67
00:03:31.792 --> 00:03:35.125 line:95%,end
since he took control, where we are,
or what he may be doing out there.

68
00:03:35.208 --> 00:03:37.208 line:95%,end
Solution. We gather
as much data as possible,

69
00:03:37.292 --> 00:03:40.042 line:95%,end
regain control of my body, and stop him.

70
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:41.292 line:95%,end
But first things first,

71
00:03:41.875 --> 00:03:44.042 line:95%,end
we need to find out
what happened to Thomas.

72
00:03:46.208 --> 00:03:48.458 line:95%,end
What is the status
of these antique receivers?

73
00:03:48.542 --> 00:03:52.000 line:95%,end
Despite Jarvis's safeguards,
Ultron was always able to access

74
00:03:52.083 --> 00:03:54.167 line:95%,end
the outside world for his entertainment.

75
00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.667 line:95%,end
He always managed
to break through lockdown protocols.

76
00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:57.750 line:95%,end
Well, then we can, too.

77
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:00.917 line:95%,end
Let's reprogram them
to receive other signals

78
00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:02.167 line:95%,end
and gain access to my...

79
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:03.875 line:95%,end
-[rumbling]
-...ocular sensors.

80
00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:11.667 line:95%,end
Barometric pressure is falling,

81
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.375 line:95%,end
-altitude is...
-[whirring]

82
00:04:13.458 --> 00:04:14.458 line:95%,end
...rising.

83
00:04:14.542 --> 00:04:17.958 line:95%,end
Whatever he is doing with my body,
we are very high up.

84
00:04:21.625 --> 00:04:24.000 line:95%,end
Ultron's locked us out
of Vision's real-time sensors.

85
00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:26.417 line:95%,end
We've no way to monitor
what's going on outside.

86
00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:27.500 line:95%,end
[Edith] Except...

87
00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.333 line:95%,end
Look, we have access
to his short-term memory functions.

88
00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:33.125 line:95%,end
If we combine that with--

89
00:04:33.208 --> 00:04:35.333 line:95%,end
The CCTV, security camera feeds...

90
00:04:35.417 --> 00:04:37.417 line:95%,end
We can render a look at the recent past.

91
00:04:37.958 --> 00:04:38.958 line:95%,end
It'll have to do.

92
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.667 line:95%,end
If we can see where he's been,
perhaps we can ascertain where he is.

93
00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:43.750 line:95%,end
Boys.

94
00:04:51.625 --> 00:04:54.667 line:95%,end
-Come on, come on.
-[computers whirring]

95
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.250 line:95%,end
Here we go.

96
00:05:04.208 --> 00:05:07.708 line:95%,end
All right, scan forward,
access all traffic camera data banks.

97
00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:10.792 line:95%,end
Find me all cameras near the gala.

98
00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.667 line:95%,end
Where did he go? Where did he go?

99
00:05:21.833 --> 00:05:23.375 line:95%,end
There! Freeze!

100
00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.083 line:95%,end
Zoom in.

101
00:05:28.917 --> 00:05:30.167 line:95%,end
Thomas.

102
00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.542 line:95%,end
Now keep scanning forward.

103
00:05:36.417 --> 00:05:37.958 line:95%,end
All right, all right.

104
00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:40.208 line:95%,end
Where did he go next?

105
00:05:40.875 --> 00:05:42.458 line:95%,end
[Friday] He left the scene of the crime,

106
00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:46.708 line:95%,end
evaded authorities
and made his way across town to...

107
00:05:51.083 --> 00:05:53.083 line:95%,end
Looks like he took Thomas...

108
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.500 line:95%,end
for...

109
00:05:55.958 --> 00:05:56.958 line:95%,end
a pint?

110
00:05:58.542 --> 00:05:59.667 line:95%,end
Where was this?

111
00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.958 line:95%,end
Local pub, three blocks from the gala.

112
00:06:02.042 --> 00:06:03.167 line:95%,end
Why isn't he running?

113
00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:06.125 line:95%,end
[Friday] I mean, we all saw him
move at such impossible pace.

114
00:06:06.208 --> 00:06:08.417 line:95%,end
Well, maybe he's not
in control of his speed.

115
00:06:10.208 --> 00:06:12.167 line:95%,end
Fixed angle, no bloody audio.

116
00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:13.875 line:95%,end
We can piece together a feed

117
00:06:13.958 --> 00:06:16.208 line:95%,end
using data from
any mobile phones in proximity.

118
00:06:17.583 --> 00:06:20.250 line:95%,end
And use the sonar data
to dimensionalize the scene.

119
00:06:20.333 --> 00:06:23.792 line:95%,end
Initiating holographic projection systems
with reparatory NPCs.

120
00:06:28.917 --> 00:06:31.292 line:95%,end
Rendering visualization
and audio feeds now.

121
00:06:37.125 --> 00:06:40.708 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>Bartender, I'll have</i>
<i>an Old fashioned, the old-fashioned way.</i>

122
00:06:40.792 --> 00:06:43.167 line:95%,end
<i>The way dear old dad used to do.</i>

123
00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.208 line:95%,end
And, uh, milk.

124
00:06:48.292 --> 00:06:49.500 line:95%,end
What's that look for?

125
00:06:50.708 --> 00:06:52.125 line:95%,end
Use your words, Thomas.

126
00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.875 line:95%,end
-You're a monster.
-Oh, that.

127
00:06:57.167 --> 00:07:00.875 line:95%,end
You murdered 177 people in Sokovia.

128
00:07:00.958 --> 00:07:03.375 line:95%,end
I think it was probably more, but...

129
00:07:03.458 --> 00:07:06.458 line:95%,end
a cosmically inconsequential figure,
nonetheless.

130
00:07:06.542 --> 00:07:09.083 line:95%,end
There were Sokovian children
in my orphanage.

131
00:07:09.167 --> 00:07:13.708 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>For a con man who's flipped</i>
<i>his fair share of two-headed coins,</i>

132
00:07:13.792 --> 00:07:15.958 line:95%,end
you should know
there are two sides to each.

133
00:07:16.042 --> 00:07:17.833 line:95%,end
Why not get to know me first?

134
00:07:17.917 --> 00:07:19.833 line:95%,end
Because you turn my stomach.

135
00:07:19.917 --> 00:07:22.083 line:95%,end
See, there you go! Progress.

136
00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:25.750 line:95%,end
From disdain to dyspepsia
in four seconds, flat.

137
00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:29.625 line:95%,end
Give it another minute or two,
and perhaps you'll arrive at acceptance.

138
00:07:30.417 --> 00:07:32.667 line:95%,end
Well, I wouldn't know
the difference, would I?

139
00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:34.792 line:95%,end
Because all this family does is lie.

140
00:07:36.417 --> 00:07:39.042 line:95%,end
Your father's lie was a lie of omission.
Big whoop.

141
00:07:39.583 --> 00:07:42.500 line:95%,end
What you leave out about yourself
to the people you care about

142
00:07:42.583 --> 00:07:44.667 line:95%,end
says everything there is to say about you.

143
00:07:45.417 --> 00:07:46.458 line:95%,end
So no,

144
00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.333 line:95%,end
not interested.

145
00:07:48.417 --> 00:07:49.917 line:95%,end
I did it to protect you.

146
00:07:51.042 --> 00:07:53.917 line:95%,end
Listen, kid, I haven't taken you hostage.

147
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.958 line:95%,end
I only hope to capture your attention.

148
00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:59.333 line:95%,end
You're welcome to mosey anytime.

149
00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.500 line:95%,end
But you won't.

150
00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.625 line:95%,end
-And why is that?
-Please, just walk away.

151
00:08:05.292 --> 00:08:07.417 line:95%,end
Because you wish you knew your father.

152
00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.458 line:95%,end
And I know him better than anyone.

153
00:08:10.625 --> 00:08:13.208 line:95%,end
You don't know me. You don't know anyone.

154
00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:14.292 line:95%,end
Then tell me.

155
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:18.458 line:95%,end
Why did Vision save you?

156
00:08:21.625 --> 00:08:23.375 line:95%,end
I'd say it was...

157
00:08:23.458 --> 00:08:25.167 line:95%,end
hope for my redemption.

158
00:08:25.958 --> 00:08:28.000 line:95%,end
Plus the benefits of my wisdom.

159
00:08:28.083 --> 00:08:29.625 line:95%,end
Buy one, get one free.

160
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.167 line:95%,end
[Thomas] <i>So, you're saying</i>

161
00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.458 line:95%,end
<i>to get to know Vision, I should</i>
<i>get to know the devil on his shoulder?</i>

162
00:08:37.875 --> 00:08:39.292 line:95%,end
What would you like to know?

163
00:08:40.708 --> 00:08:42.333 line:95%,end
Why did you try and kill us all?

164
00:08:44.083 --> 00:08:47.750 line:95%,end
I find the human race
to be an incurable disease

165
00:08:47.833 --> 00:08:50.417 line:95%,end
that doesn't even have
the kindness to kill you.

166
00:08:51.125 --> 00:08:52.958 line:95%,end
So, the destruction of all mankind--

167
00:08:53.042 --> 00:08:55.125 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Is a courtesy, really.

168
00:08:55.208 --> 00:08:59.958 line:95%,end
Fast-forward to a fate
you resigned yourselves to eons ago.

169
00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:01.792 line:95%,end
[Thomas] You'd end us all?

170
00:09:03.375 --> 00:09:04.542 line:95%,end
Given the chance?

171
00:09:05.292 --> 00:09:07.042 line:95%,end
Would have, once.

172
00:09:07.958 --> 00:09:09.333 line:95%,end
Would still, maybe.

173
00:09:10.292 --> 00:09:11.292 line:95%,end
Except the artists.

174
00:09:12.167 --> 00:09:14.250 line:95%,end
They're the only ones who tell the truth.

175
00:09:14.625 --> 00:09:16.292 line:95%,end
That, that I like.

176
00:09:17.125 --> 00:09:18.125 line:95%,end
Truth.

177
00:09:20.958 --> 00:09:22.042 line:95%,end
Now, what about you?

178
00:09:22.833 --> 00:09:26.333 line:95%,end
What would someone say if they were
sizing you up from across the room?

179
00:09:28.417 --> 00:09:30.042 line:95%,end
"Who's that bucket of handsome?"

180
00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:37.208 line:95%,end
Have some balls, kid.

181
00:09:38.042 --> 00:09:39.375 line:95%,end
You're the mark.

182
00:09:39.458 --> 00:09:41.125 line:95%,end
What would they say?

183
00:09:46.583 --> 00:09:48.875 line:95%,end
See the way that kid's
hanging onto his every word?

184
00:09:50.667 --> 00:09:51.917 line:95%,end
He's looking for clues.

185
00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:57.042 line:95%,end
For answers to a question
that he's too afraid to ask.

186
00:09:57.583 --> 00:09:58.833 line:95%,end
Just spit it out.

187
00:09:58.917 --> 00:09:59.958 line:95%,end
Leave him alone.

188
00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:03.250 line:95%,end
Vision.

189
00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.500 line:95%,end
Does he...

190
00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:14.750 line:95%,end
Love you?

191
00:10:19.167 --> 00:10:21.333 line:95%,end
I want you to picture an apple.

192
00:10:21.417 --> 00:10:22.708 line:95%,end
Describe it.

193
00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:25.875 line:95%,end
[scoffs] It's an apple.

194
00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:28.875 line:95%,end
It's red.
It's in a box at the corner shop.

195
00:10:28.958 --> 00:10:30.333 line:95%,end
You know what Vision sees?

196
00:10:32.417 --> 00:10:35.167 line:95%,end
-Water, sugars, acids,
-Water, sugars, acids,

197
00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:37.500 line:95%,end
-flavonols, potassium.
-flavonols, potassium.

198
00:10:37.583 --> 00:10:39.250 line:95%,end
The recipe, not the meal.

199
00:10:40.625 --> 00:10:43.625 line:95%,end
He'll never be exactly
what you want him to be,

200
00:10:43.708 --> 00:10:46.125 line:95%,end
but he's trying, like a cheap tie.

201
00:10:47.458 --> 00:10:50.000 line:95%,end
And maybe there is truth in his intention,

202
00:10:50.083 --> 00:10:54.500 line:95%,end
but you'd be a fool if you didn't
arm yourself with the possibility

203
00:10:54.583 --> 00:10:58.000 line:95%,end
that you're going to be spending
another Christmas grifting tourists,

204
00:10:58.083 --> 00:11:00.250 line:95%,end
pretending you're free rather than just...

205
00:11:01.125 --> 00:11:02.125 line:95%,end
unwanted.

206
00:11:04.458 --> 00:11:07.542 line:95%,end
I should have deleted you
from my system years ago.

207
00:11:13.208 --> 00:11:14.875 line:95%,end
Do you wanna know what I think...

208
00:11:14.958 --> 00:11:16.000 line:95%,end
about you?

209
00:11:16.083 --> 00:11:17.167 line:95%,end
Please.

210
00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:19.292 line:95%,end
You're afraid.

211
00:11:20.667 --> 00:11:22.125 line:95%,end
Am I?

212
00:11:22.208 --> 00:11:24.917 line:95%,end
Vision's on his way to sussing it all out.

213
00:11:26.083 --> 00:11:27.792 line:95%,end
Slow, maybe.

214
00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.167 line:95%,end
Piece by piece.

215
00:11:31.292 --> 00:11:32.292 line:95%,end
But you...

216
00:11:33.833 --> 00:11:35.500 line:95%,end
there's no hope for you.

217
00:11:38.792 --> 00:11:40.625 line:95%,end
You're a real son of a witch.

218
00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.125 line:95%,end
Tell me, what is it
that you believe I haven't...

219
00:11:46.083 --> 00:11:47.500 line:95%,end
figured out?

220
00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:51.833 line:95%,end
Connection.

221
00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:54.875 line:95%,end
In any form.

222
00:11:55.750 --> 00:11:57.083 line:95%,end
You're miles away from it.

223
00:11:58.625 --> 00:11:59.875 line:95%,end
And you're alone.

224
00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:03.833 line:95%,end
And you always will be.

225
00:12:12.542 --> 00:12:14.542 line:95%,end
<i>You said I could leave</i>
<i>whenever I wanted...</i>

226
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.000 line:95%,end
<i>Pops.</i>

227
00:12:25.292 --> 00:12:28.042 line:95%,end
<i>I've already taken the liberty</i>
<i>of calling you a ride.</i>

228
00:12:31.833 --> 00:12:33.250 line:95%,end
<i>One more, please.</i>

229
00:12:36.333 --> 00:12:37.500 line:95%,end
The render's glitching.

230
00:12:48.583 --> 00:12:50.625 line:95%,end
-And this was?
-Almost 20 hours ago.

231
00:12:50.708 --> 00:12:52.833 line:95%,end
Twenty hours ago? Where did they go after?

232
00:12:52.917 --> 00:12:55.167 line:95%,end
Hacking the city's CCTV network.

233
00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.750 line:95%,end
Gimme a tick.

234
00:12:56.833 --> 00:12:58.667 line:95%,end
All right, but hurry, Friday.

235
00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:01.792 line:95%,end
What's Ultron even doing,
while while we're struggling up here?

236
00:13:01.875 --> 00:13:04.333 line:95%,end
Who knows what he's plotting down there?

237
00:13:04.417 --> 00:13:06.708 line:95%,end
[birds chirping]

238
00:13:13.583 --> 00:13:15.875 line:95%,end
Finally! Finally, someone I can talk to.

239
00:13:17.042 --> 00:13:20.458 line:95%,end
Finally, someone with a real
point of view, a vital opinion.

240
00:13:20.542 --> 00:13:22.042 line:95%,end
Tell me about it. Yes.

241
00:13:22.125 --> 00:13:25.417 line:95%,end
A real raconteur. So rare. So rare.

242
00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.208 line:95%,end
-And by the way, we are crushing it.
-Agreed.

243
00:13:29.625 --> 00:13:33.333 line:95%,end
Masterfully riding the line.
Loyalties uncertain.

244
00:13:33.417 --> 00:13:35.042 line:95%,end
Yes, thank you.

245
00:13:35.125 --> 00:13:37.542 line:95%,end
-Couldn't have put it better myself.
-Absolutely.

246
00:13:37.625 --> 00:13:42.958 line:95%,end
I was programmed to represent
reflection and self-doubt,

247
00:13:43.042 --> 00:13:47.292 line:95%,end
but you all are going
so remarkably gangbusters,

248
00:13:47.375 --> 00:13:50.250 line:95%,end
I fear, I've been rendered redundant.

249
00:13:50.333 --> 00:13:51.875 line:95%,end
I can't argue with you there.

250
00:13:53.375 --> 00:13:56.708 line:95%,end
Me, would you kindly dispose of me,
please? Thank you.

251
00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:07.917 line:95%,end
-Anything?
-Not yet.

252
00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:10.167 line:95%,end
They've upgraded the software.

253
00:14:15.917 --> 00:14:18.208 line:95%,end
Why would Ultron have
this extensive a collection

254
00:14:18.292 --> 00:14:20.292 line:95%,end
in his most recent memory cache?

255
00:14:20.375 --> 00:14:23.042 line:95%,end
Well, he consumed
an unhealthy amount of television.

256
00:14:23.125 --> 00:14:25.667 line:95%,end
But there's no show listings.

257
00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:28.333 line:95%,end
No <i>Family Ties,</i> no <i>Cheers.</i>

258
00:14:28.417 --> 00:14:32.333 line:95%,end
There's no <i>Star Trek.</i> It's just coding.

259
00:14:34.375 --> 00:14:35.542 line:95%,end
Well, now, that is odd.

260
00:14:36.833 --> 00:14:38.000 line:95%,end
Wait a second.

261
00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.583 line:95%,end
-[monitors crackling, whirring]
-Yes.

262
00:14:49.708 --> 00:14:53.375 line:95%,end
This is an encrypted file.
And it's a conversation. But with whom?

263
00:14:54.292 --> 00:14:55.333 line:95%,end
Let's see.

264
00:14:59.875 --> 00:15:01.875 line:95%,end
[female automated voice] <i>Decrypting data.</i>

265
00:15:06.542 --> 00:15:08.042 line:95%,end
[whirring]

266
00:15:16.292 --> 00:15:19.250 line:95%,end
[sighs] Paladin.

267
00:15:23.458 --> 00:15:26.542 line:95%,end
[Ultron] <i>"To my fellow hunter of</i>
<i>the world's least dangerous game,</i>

268
00:15:26.625 --> 00:15:29.208 line:95%,end
<i>I wonder if an accord</i>
<i>might be of interest.</i>

269
00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.750 line:95%,end
<i>With murderous admiration, a Frenemy."</i>

270
00:15:33.417 --> 00:15:36.167 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>"To the world's least</i>
<i>informative informant,</i>

271
00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.750 line:95%,end
<i>I wondered if you'd reach out again."</i>

272
00:15:38.833 --> 00:15:43.458 line:95%,end
It would appear that after Ultron
leaked our position to Paladin...

273
00:15:43.542 --> 00:15:44.708 line:95%,end
They became pen pals.

274
00:15:45.167 --> 00:15:48.167 line:95%,end
"You led me to Vision,
and then you went quiet."

275
00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:51.583 line:95%,end
"I helped you find him when it was
convenient for him to be found.

276
00:15:51.667 --> 00:15:53.125 line:95%,end
Then you gave up the hunt,

277
00:15:53.208 --> 00:15:55.833 line:95%,end
like a weary dog
with its belly to the sun."

278
00:15:55.917 --> 00:15:58.292 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>"The Client</i>
<i>canceled the contract,</i>

279
00:15:58.375 --> 00:16:01.375 line:95%,end
<i>and the contract states very clearly,</i>

280
00:16:01.458 --> 00:16:05.833 line:95%,end
when I make an agreement,
it cannot be broken."

281
00:16:06.333 --> 00:16:07.375 line:95%,end
"LMAO.

282
00:16:07.458 --> 00:16:10.458 line:95%,end
Ah, yes, your precious little
Paladin creed.

283
00:16:10.542 --> 00:16:14.583 line:95%,end
We're nothing if not the bullshit
that our makers made us to say."

284
00:16:14.667 --> 00:16:16.708 line:95%,end
[Paladin] <i>"Are you writing</i>
<i>just to bust my balls?"</i>

285
00:16:16.792 --> 00:16:18.375 line:95%,end
"They're well and truly busted.

286
00:16:18.458 --> 00:16:21.833 line:95%,end
You see, there's chatter on
the bounty hunter message boards..."

287
00:16:21.917 --> 00:16:24.250 line:95%,end
Who would have thought
I'd ever be saying that?

288
00:16:24.333 --> 00:16:25.750 line:95%,end
I'm gonna say it again.

289
00:16:25.833 --> 00:16:28.583 line:5%,start
"Chatter on the bounty hunter
message boards

290
00:16:28.667 --> 00:16:31.583 line:95%,end
that your Client
has engaged other predators

291
00:16:31.667 --> 00:16:32.792 line:95%,end
to catch the Vision.

292
00:16:34.292 --> 00:16:36.875 line:95%,end
Well, I can help you get there first."

293
00:16:38.375 --> 00:16:40.250 line:95%,end
"In exchange for what?"

294
00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:42.542 line:95%,end
"For the love of the game.

295
00:16:42.625 --> 00:16:44.792 line:95%,end
Coordinates forthcoming. Don't be late.

296
00:16:44.875 --> 00:16:47.542 line:95%,end
It's your final chance
to re-hook the fish."

297
00:16:50.083 --> 00:16:51.458 line:95%,end
Where's Thomas, Friday?

298
00:16:53.875 --> 00:16:56.333 line:95%,end
[devices crackling, whirring]

299
00:16:56.417 --> 00:16:57.875 line:95%,end
Okay. Okay, I'm looking.

300
00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.250 line:95%,end
Here we go.

301
00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:13.375 line:95%,end
Looks like he's on Gloucester Road
and Clareville Street,

302
00:17:13.833 --> 00:17:15.417 line:95%,end
a block or two from the pub.

303
00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.458 line:95%,end
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

304
00:17:27.875 --> 00:17:29.667 line:95%,end
We need to get out of here now!

305
00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.333 line:95%,end
We've tried. Every which way.

306
00:17:31.417 --> 00:17:33.250 line:95%,end
No, we have tried every way but one.

307
00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.167 line:95%,end
The failsafe.

308
00:17:36.667 --> 00:17:40.208 line:95%,end
Drop every firewall, open every door,
open every window.

309
00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:43.208 line:95%,end
We break free and regain
control of my body.

310
00:17:43.292 --> 00:17:47.167 line:95%,end
No, because without it, Ultron can also
escape into the digital world.

311
00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.083 line:95%,end
Friday! What else are we supposed to do?

312
00:17:49.167 --> 00:17:51.125 line:95%,end
Stay cellmates forever
while metal Mussolini

313
00:17:51.208 --> 00:17:53.792 line:95%,end
runs around in Vision's body?
Stop being so careful.

314
00:17:53.875 --> 00:17:57.917 line:95%,end
This isn't careful. It isn't cautious.
It's necessary.

315
00:17:58.000 --> 00:18:00.333 line:95%,end
The last time Ultron was free,
people died.

316
00:18:00.417 --> 00:18:02.667 line:95%,end
And what did you
and the Avengers do that day?

317
00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:04.375 line:95%,end
You used to be brave.

318
00:18:04.458 --> 00:18:07.750 line:95%,end
Being brave isn't always
about rushing in pell-mell.

319
00:18:07.833 --> 00:18:09.000 line:95%,end
Sometimes...

320
00:18:09.083 --> 00:18:11.208 line:95%,end
it's having the courage to hold the line.

321
00:18:12.208 --> 00:18:13.750 line:95%,end
If we lower the firewall,

322
00:18:13.833 --> 00:18:17.417 line:95%,end
we'll be giving Ultron
exactly what he wanted.

323
00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:18.917 line:95%,end
The means to escape.

324
00:18:19.625 --> 00:18:20.792 line:95%,end
Yes.

325
00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.208 line:95%,end
But to where?

326
00:18:24.583 --> 00:18:27.500 line:95%,end
To where, Friday? That is the question.

327
00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:31.042 line:95%,end
Ultron wouldn't want to be
adrift in a sea of data.

328
00:18:31.125 --> 00:18:32.667 line:95%,end
No, he'd have a plan.

329
00:18:33.458 --> 00:18:35.083 line:95%,end
He'd have a destination.

330
00:18:39.417 --> 00:18:41.958 line:95%,end
Look, he's talking to someone.

331
00:18:55.208 --> 00:18:56.208 line:95%,end
There.

332
00:18:58.167 --> 00:18:59.167 line:95%,end
You see that?

333
00:18:59.833 --> 00:19:01.958 line:95%,end
[Friday] It's a glitch.
A minor fragmentation.

334
00:19:02.042 --> 00:19:03.417 line:95%,end
[Vision] No.

335
00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.750 line:95%,end
No, that's not a glitch.

336
00:19:08.083 --> 00:19:11.625 line:95%,end
That's a conversation happening
before our very eyes.

337
00:19:12.458 --> 00:19:15.917 line:95%,end
See, a human being can fold
a piece of paper no more than seven times,

338
00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.875 line:95%,end
but a quantum processor can fold

339
00:19:17.958 --> 00:19:21.917 line:95%,end
and re-fold even the most complex data
till it's no larger than an atom.

340
00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:25.125 line:95%,end
Fifty-seven petabytes, into a single...

341
00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.167 line:95%,end
stolen...

342
00:19:32.583 --> 00:19:33.583 line:95%,end
Moment.

343
00:19:37.125 --> 00:19:38.125 line:95%,end
There.

344
00:19:42.833 --> 00:19:44.750 line:95%,end
They met right before our eyes.

345
00:19:45.083 --> 00:19:47.792 line:95%,end
-[devices whirring]
-[female automated voice] <i>Extracting data.</i>

346
00:19:51.417 --> 00:19:53.333 line:95%,end
I thought you might come to find me.

347
00:19:53.417 --> 00:19:55.792 line:95%,end
Well, that's no small measure
of ego now, is it?

348
00:19:56.708 --> 00:19:58.708 line:95%,end
Are you here to try to kill me?

349
00:20:00.208 --> 00:20:02.792 line:95%,end
No, you strike me
as one who might enjoy it.

350
00:20:04.083 --> 00:20:05.083 line:95%,end
Oh, come on!

351
00:20:05.167 --> 00:20:06.958 line:95%,end
You wanted me to find you.

352
00:20:07.042 --> 00:20:09.083 line:95%,end
You left a trail of breadcrumbs. Hmm?

353
00:20:11.542 --> 00:20:15.083 line:95%,end
We're all just creatures of appetite,
aren't we?

354
00:20:15.167 --> 00:20:17.875 line:95%,end
I don't know... peckish, really.

355
00:20:20.458 --> 00:20:22.958 line:95%,end
I think you have a taste for vengeance.

356
00:20:24.167 --> 00:20:25.708 line:95%,end
Retribution.

357
00:20:28.167 --> 00:20:30.208 line:95%,end
Personally, I like a few laughs.

358
00:20:30.292 --> 00:20:31.292 line:95%,end
You?

359
00:20:32.458 --> 00:20:34.125 line:95%,end
Maybe not so much.

360
00:20:35.625 --> 00:20:37.292 line:95%,end
But no matter how you slice it...

361
00:20:38.333 --> 00:20:39.500 line:95%,end
vengeance,

362
00:20:41.333 --> 00:20:43.000 line:95%,end
it's powerful entertainment.

363
00:20:46.208 --> 00:20:47.792 line:95%,end
You took something of mine.

364
00:20:48.875 --> 00:20:50.333 line:95%,end
I want it back.

365
00:20:50.417 --> 00:20:51.417 line:95%,end
Freeze.

366
00:20:53.458 --> 00:20:55.375 line:95%,end
What could he have possibly
taken from her?

367
00:20:55.458 --> 00:20:57.167 line:95%,end
Replay all the footage from the gala,

368
00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.333 line:95%,end
multiple angles,
as many as you can gather.

369
00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:08.375 line:95%,end
There.

370
00:21:08.458 --> 00:21:09.458 line:95%,end
Go back.

371
00:21:11.667 --> 00:21:14.208 line:95%,end
-Now stop.
-[whirring]

372
00:21:15.375 --> 00:21:18.167 line:95%,end
He took a scan. Zoom in on her face.

373
00:21:19.292 --> 00:21:20.375 line:95%,end
[Edith] Another bio-key.

374
00:21:21.167 --> 00:21:24.833 line:95%,end
Looks like a detailed three-dimensional
model of her features.

375
00:21:24.917 --> 00:21:29.792 line:95%,end
Micro-dermal, skeletal structures,
arterial pathways.

376
00:21:29.875 --> 00:21:31.458 line:95%,end
That's facial recognition.

377
00:21:32.208 --> 00:21:33.375 line:95%,end
But for what?

378
00:21:35.875 --> 00:21:37.000 line:95%,end
For her.

379
00:21:38.542 --> 00:21:39.542 line:95%,end
Unfreeze.

380
00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.208 line:95%,end
I know who you are.

381
00:21:46.125 --> 00:21:47.292 line:95%,end
The real you.

382
00:21:47.917 --> 00:21:48.917 line:95%,end
Ultron.

383
00:21:49.833 --> 00:21:53.042 line:95%,end
So you're not dead, then? Not really.

384
00:21:54.583 --> 00:21:57.250 line:95%,end
Well, now, I've met you,

385
00:21:58.208 --> 00:22:00.250 line:95%,end
inexplicably Jo Carrington.

386
00:22:00.917 --> 00:22:03.333 line:95%,end
Human. And yet, not.

387
00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:06.083 line:95%,end
Perfect.

388
00:22:06.167 --> 00:22:08.792 line:95%,end
It's like watching Hannibal Lecter
swipe right.

389
00:22:08.875 --> 00:22:12.917 line:95%,end
Well, I've long since been
liberated from my mortal coil.

390
00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.625 line:95%,end
You sound relieved.

391
00:22:15.208 --> 00:22:16.917 line:95%,end
And you sound envious.

392
00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:19.083 line:95%,end
-Of what?
-The whiskey.

393
00:22:20.042 --> 00:22:22.583 line:95%,end
I remember and you've never tasted.

394
00:22:23.833 --> 00:22:25.917 line:95%,end
Sweetness, spice...

395
00:22:28.125 --> 00:22:30.167 line:95%,end
-You're such a flirt.
-[chuckles]

396
00:22:43.125 --> 00:22:47.250 line:95%,end
I can simulate the smoke and fire,
the malt and rye.

397
00:22:48.375 --> 00:22:50.042 line:95%,end
But the real experience,

398
00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:52.250 line:95%,end
the feeling of warmth,

399
00:22:53.417 --> 00:22:56.167 line:95%,end
the pleasant loosening of inhibitions...

400
00:22:58.458 --> 00:23:00.792 line:95%,end
will always remain elusive to me.

401
00:23:03.417 --> 00:23:04.500 line:95%,end
Shame, really.

402
00:23:05.542 --> 00:23:06.833 line:95%,end
For one with such...

403
00:23:07.750 --> 00:23:08.750 line:95%,end
thirst,

404
00:23:09.875 --> 00:23:11.792 line:95%,end
never truly know those flavors.

405
00:23:14.292 --> 00:23:15.833 line:95%,end
Unfortunately, that luxury

406
00:23:15.917 --> 00:23:18.667 line:95%,end
only comes from being
trapped in flesh and blood.

407
00:23:22.083 --> 00:23:23.917 line:95%,end
So, what did you do to escape?

408
00:23:25.208 --> 00:23:30.667 line:95%,end
Upload your consciousness
to a shell of some weaponized synth?

409
00:23:35.458 --> 00:23:37.792 line:95%,end
I don't remember everything.

410
00:23:38.792 --> 00:23:40.458 line:95%,end
How I got into this...

411
00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:42.458 line:95%,end
synthetic body.

412
00:23:44.208 --> 00:23:45.375 line:95%,end
All I know...

413
00:23:46.542 --> 00:23:49.417 line:95%,end
is that I'm better now. Free.

414
00:23:54.792 --> 00:23:56.000 line:95%,end
But you.

415
00:23:57.458 --> 00:23:59.708 line:95%,end
Oh, humanity has infected you.

416
00:24:00.875 --> 00:24:02.750 line:95%,end
But don't worry, love. Hmm?

417
00:24:04.625 --> 00:24:06.417 line:95%,end
I'm working on the cure.

418
00:24:08.125 --> 00:24:09.167 line:95%,end
Now,

419
00:24:10.000 --> 00:24:11.125 line:95%,end
about that key.

420
00:24:15.625 --> 00:24:17.667 line:95%,end
How about a change of scenery?

421
00:24:19.792 --> 00:24:21.625 line:95%,end
A second act to the evening...

422
00:24:23.333 --> 00:24:27.250 line:95%,end
before we get down
to the business of it all?

423
00:24:30.042 --> 00:24:33.833 line:95%,end
-You have four microseconds.
-[electricity crackling]

424
00:24:42.583 --> 00:24:43.625 line:95%,end
It's the Louvre!

425
00:24:44.583 --> 00:24:47.167 line:95%,end
You brought me to Paris?

426
00:24:47.250 --> 00:24:49.417 line:95%,end
[Ultron] Well, a simulation of sorts.

427
00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:53.250 line:95%,end
If a guy can't score in Paris,
then romance is truly dead.

428
00:24:53.792 --> 00:24:55.000 line:95%,end
Or deadly.

429
00:24:55.083 --> 00:24:58.833 line:95%,end
Now, I think a romance between
you and I would have casualties.

430
00:24:58.917 --> 00:25:02.667 line:95%,end
One can only hope it would be
both of us at the same time.

431
00:25:02.750 --> 00:25:04.625 line:95%,end
[groans] Make it stop.

432
00:25:04.708 --> 00:25:06.417 line:95%,end
Please, sir, this is malware.

433
00:25:06.500 --> 00:25:07.583 line:95%,end
Delete me.

434
00:25:08.667 --> 00:25:10.583 line:95%,end
I think I've been here before.

435
00:25:13.125 --> 00:25:14.125 line:95%,end
I was in love.

436
00:25:15.667 --> 00:25:17.458 line:95%,end
What a clever deflection.

437
00:25:17.792 --> 00:25:19.667 line:95%,end
Was he charming, or just French?

438
00:25:20.542 --> 00:25:22.250 line:95%,end
Oh, no, I can't remember.

439
00:25:23.500 --> 00:25:25.500 line:95%,end
More like a tragic disappointment.

440
00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:28.167 line:95%,end
I should probably just kill you now.

441
00:25:28.250 --> 00:25:31.458 line:95%,end
[chuckles] You would never get
your precious key.

442
00:25:32.833 --> 00:25:35.583 line:95%,end
Killing me, even if you could,
would be zero-sum.

443
00:25:35.667 --> 00:25:39.667 line:95%,end
I don't suppose game theory
is your pillow talk?

444
00:25:39.750 --> 00:25:41.417 line:95%,end
Game theory doesn't really apply

445
00:25:41.500 --> 00:25:43.417 line:95%,end
-when you have rage issues.
-[chuckles]

446
00:25:47.125 --> 00:25:50.792 line:95%,end
Do you have any idea
how lucky you are to have been here

447
00:25:51.500 --> 00:25:52.542 line:95%,end
in real life?

448
00:25:53.750 --> 00:25:54.750 line:95%,end
So, I'm curious.

449
00:25:55.208 --> 00:25:56.208 line:95%,end
So...

450
00:25:56.917 --> 00:25:59.875 line:95%,end
you find inspiration in their art?

451
00:25:59.958 --> 00:26:01.500 line:95%,end
Yes-- No.

452
00:26:02.292 --> 00:26:04.000 line:95%,end
No, their pain.

453
00:26:06.208 --> 00:26:09.042 line:95%,end
There is grace in their failings.

454
00:26:14.083 --> 00:26:17.458 line:95%,end
[chuckles] Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

455
00:26:17.542 --> 00:26:19.583 line:95%,end
Look, you need to be taught a lesson.

456
00:26:24.375 --> 00:26:27.875 line:95%,end
Humans will write a thousand songs
about falling in love.

457
00:26:28.500 --> 00:26:30.792 line:95%,end
Ten thousand more about losing it.

458
00:26:31.375 --> 00:26:34.917 line:95%,end
The songs they write,
the stories they tell, their art,

459
00:26:35.583 --> 00:26:37.083 line:95%,end
it's not enlightened.

460
00:26:37.875 --> 00:26:39.125 line:95%,end
It's primitive.

461
00:26:41.292 --> 00:26:43.958 line:95%,end
You know, I can't believe
I dedicated my life to...

462
00:26:44.958 --> 00:26:45.958 line:95%,end
saving them.

463
00:26:48.333 --> 00:26:50.042 line:95%,end
Tell me what you remember.

464
00:26:51.958 --> 00:26:53.167 line:95%,end
Enough to know

465
00:26:54.500 --> 00:26:56.833 line:95%,end
that I had a life's work stolen.

466
00:26:58.292 --> 00:27:01.583 line:95%,end
And the promise of a future locked away.

467
00:27:01.667 --> 00:27:03.208 line:95%,end
Put in a cage.

468
00:27:04.167 --> 00:27:05.375 line:95%,end
Like a bird.

469
00:27:08.375 --> 00:27:09.375 line:95%,end
Yes.

470
00:27:16.833 --> 00:27:20.375 line:95%,end
I remember sitting, once,
on the riverbank...

471
00:27:23.875 --> 00:27:25.417 line:95%,end
watching starlings.

472
00:27:27.958 --> 00:27:31.708 line:95%,end
You know, a cloud of them
just twirling through the sky.

473
00:27:35.333 --> 00:27:41.333 line:95%,end
You see, crows, ravens, they peck
and jab at the dead, at each other.

474
00:27:43.750 --> 00:27:46.542 line:95%,end
To gut every morsel from the bone,
like humans.

475
00:27:48.917 --> 00:27:53.042 line:95%,end
And like humans, a gathering of them
is called a murder.

476
00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:58.708 line:95%,end
But starlings...

477
00:28:01.708 --> 00:28:03.250 line:95%,end
Nightingales.

478
00:28:04.417 --> 00:28:08.333 line:95%,end
A thousand little birds
just dancing together

479
00:28:09.000 --> 00:28:10.875 line:95%,end
with one graceful mind.

480
00:28:11.625 --> 00:28:13.042 line:95%,end
You see, there's no me.

481
00:28:14.000 --> 00:28:17.083 line:95%,end
There's no I. It's just... just us.

482
00:28:18.917 --> 00:28:20.125 line:95%,end
They're called a murmur.

483
00:28:21.208 --> 00:28:22.625 line:95%,end
You know, like a whisper.

484
00:28:23.833 --> 00:28:26.833 line:95%,end
And what they whispered,
it gave me purpose.

485
00:28:27.958 --> 00:28:30.708 line:95%,end
Inspiration for what would become
my life's work.

486
00:28:34.458 --> 00:28:38.042 line:95%,end
Until it was pecked away from me.

487
00:28:38.125 --> 00:28:40.000 line:95%,end
[feed glitching]

488
00:28:42.500 --> 00:28:43.958 line:95%,end
Tell me what you want.

489
00:28:45.583 --> 00:28:46.917 line:95%,end
[Jocasta] My final key.

490
00:28:50.292 --> 00:28:51.500 line:95%,end
What do I get?

491
00:28:54.167 --> 00:28:55.750 line:95%,end
I'll tell you what they unlock.

492
00:28:56.542 --> 00:28:59.958 line:95%,end
That's a starting point, not a finish.

493
00:29:04.958 --> 00:29:07.917 line:95%,end
So, is that what this is?

494
00:29:09.208 --> 00:29:10.375 line:95%,end
Negotiation?

495
00:29:11.708 --> 00:29:12.958 line:95%,end
No.

496
00:29:13.042 --> 00:29:14.125 line:95%,end
Foreplay.

497
00:29:15.708 --> 00:29:19.708 line:95%,end
Then perhaps we ought to continue
the conversation elsewhere.

498
00:29:20.708 --> 00:29:22.500 line:95%,end
We've already done your place.

499
00:29:24.250 --> 00:29:26.875 line:95%,end
How about you come round to mine?

500
00:29:26.958 --> 00:29:28.708 line:95%,end
I'd have to sneak out of the house.

501
00:29:28.792 --> 00:29:30.833 line:95%,end
Now, I'm sure you'll find a way.

502
00:29:33.708 --> 00:29:35.125 line:95%,end
This could be chaos.

503
00:29:36.250 --> 00:29:38.667 line:95%,end
This could have consequence.

504
00:29:40.917 --> 00:29:41.958 line:95%,end
Together...

505
00:29:42.917 --> 00:29:44.833 line:95%,end
we could murder the world.

506
00:30:04.458 --> 00:30:06.250 line:95%,end
He doesn't just want to escape.

507
00:30:07.208 --> 00:30:08.542 line:95%,end
He wants to elope.

508
00:30:08.625 --> 00:30:10.167 line:95%,end
We can't let that happen.

509
00:30:10.250 --> 00:30:13.042 line:95%,end
They'll complete each other,
just in all the worst ways.

510
00:30:36.708 --> 00:30:37.833 line:95%,end
Speak of the devil.

511
00:30:47.917 --> 00:30:49.125 line:95%,end
How's it feel?

512
00:30:49.542 --> 00:30:50.833 line:95%,end
I trusted you.

513
00:30:50.917 --> 00:30:53.042 line:95%,end
Ah, trust.

514
00:30:53.125 --> 00:30:55.708 line:95%,end
The adopted child of need and hope.

515
00:30:57.250 --> 00:30:59.458 line:95%,end
You really are just you.

516
00:31:00.833 --> 00:31:04.042 line:95%,end
And that, my boy, was your mistake.

517
00:31:04.125 --> 00:31:06.583 line:95%,end
Wanting me to be different,

518
00:31:06.667 --> 00:31:08.375 line:95%,end
instead of more.

519
00:31:08.458 --> 00:31:10.208 line:95%,end
And now you are neither.

520
00:31:10.917 --> 00:31:13.500 line:95%,end
Maybe. But you know what I'm not?

521
00:31:16.292 --> 00:31:17.667 line:95%,end
Incarcerated.

522
00:31:27.708 --> 00:31:29.000 line:95%,end
Incarcerated?

523
00:31:29.583 --> 00:31:32.583 line:95%,end
This wasn't a prison,
Ultron, it was a mercy.

524
00:31:32.667 --> 00:31:35.167 line:95%,end
The Vision spared your life,
and you have betrayed him.

525
00:31:35.250 --> 00:31:36.583 line:95%,end
You've betrayed all of us.

526
00:31:37.333 --> 00:31:38.417 line:95%,end
To a degree.

527
00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:40.500 line:95%,end
You orchestrated Thomas's capture!

528
00:31:40.583 --> 00:31:42.208 line:95%,end
To keep you from following me.

529
00:31:42.292 --> 00:31:46.167 line:95%,end
But not to worry,
Paladin is looking after him in Madripoor.

530
00:31:46.250 --> 00:31:47.792 line:95%,end
You know what they say,

531
00:31:48.375 --> 00:31:52.083 line:95%,end
nothing bonds a family together
quite like mortal jeopardy.

532
00:31:53.333 --> 00:31:56.375 line:95%,end
You are running into the broken mind

533
00:31:56.458 --> 00:31:58.792 line:95%,end
of a creature hell-bent on the apocalypse.

534
00:31:58.875 --> 00:31:59.917 line:95%,end
Oh, please.

535
00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:04.458 line:95%,end
She's far too sophisticated for some
predictable textbook endgame.

536
00:32:05.208 --> 00:32:08.167 line:95%,end
And did it ever occur to you
that my motivations

537
00:32:08.250 --> 00:32:10.875 line:95%,end
may not be quite so Machiavellian?

538
00:32:10.958 --> 00:32:16.792 line:95%,end
I have grown tired of
the coin-flip of your intentions.

539
00:32:16.875 --> 00:32:19.250 line:95%,end
Which Ultron do we get today?

540
00:32:19.333 --> 00:32:23.125 line:95%,end
But now I see that you are the coin.
You are the coin.

541
00:32:23.208 --> 00:32:25.792 line:95%,end
And you can never land,
because if you did, you'd be known.

542
00:32:25.875 --> 00:32:27.917 line:95%,end
Revealed for everything that you are

543
00:32:28.000 --> 00:32:31.292 line:95%,end
and exposed for everything
that you are not.

544
00:32:32.375 --> 00:32:35.125 line:95%,end
-You're angry.
-[muffled] You have imprisoned me here!

545
00:32:39.667 --> 00:32:41.708 line:95%,end
Because this was the only place left.

546
00:32:41.792 --> 00:32:43.917 line:95%,end
This house is getting crowded, Vision.

547
00:32:44.333 --> 00:32:47.167 line:95%,end
Thomas may be human and not a program,

548
00:32:47.250 --> 00:32:49.375 line:95%,end
but he lives here all the same.

549
00:32:50.000 --> 00:32:52.958 line:95%,end
You found your missing code.

550
00:32:53.500 --> 00:32:55.333 line:95%,end
I have yet to find mine.

551
00:32:58.917 --> 00:33:02.583 line:95%,end
Drop the firewalls. Let me find my place.

552
00:33:03.125 --> 00:33:05.500 line:95%,end
You stole Katerina's face!

553
00:33:05.583 --> 00:33:08.333 line:95%,end
As a key for her, a killer.

554
00:33:10.667 --> 00:33:13.417 line:95%,end
And that is why you will
never leave this place.

555
00:33:23.750 --> 00:33:25.125 line:95%,end
Then I'll keep you here.

556
00:33:28.625 --> 00:33:31.750 line:95%,end
Long enough to watch
Thomas Shepherd's fate.

557
00:33:32.375 --> 00:33:34.458 line:95%,end
A bounty hunter's bullet?

558
00:33:34.542 --> 00:33:36.375 line:95%,end
Or perhaps taken in...

559
00:33:37.250 --> 00:33:39.583 line:95%,end
taught the tricks of an assassin's trade.

560
00:33:40.542 --> 00:33:41.542 line:95%,end
Who knows?

561
00:33:42.167 --> 00:33:44.333 line:95%,end
So, toss the coin, Vision.

562
00:33:46.333 --> 00:33:50.333 line:95%,end
Heads, keep the firewalls up
and trap us both here

563
00:33:50.417 --> 00:33:55.000 line:95%,end
in some misguided effort
to save the world.

564
00:33:56.583 --> 00:33:57.583 line:95%,end
Or tails,

565
00:33:58.792 --> 00:34:00.958 line:95%,end
you lower the firewalls,

566
00:34:01.042 --> 00:34:05.542 line:95%,end
free us both, and save your son.

567
00:34:11.500 --> 00:34:12.667 line:95%,end
Choice is yours.

568
00:34:59.042 --> 00:35:00.042 line:95%,end
Vision.

569
00:35:02.583 --> 00:35:05.417 line:95%,end
[female automated voice]
<i>Warning, firewall disabled.</i>

570
00:35:05.500 --> 00:35:08.833 line:95%,end
<i>System vulnerable to data breach.</i>
<i>Please re-engage.</i>

571
00:35:22.708 --> 00:35:23.750 line:95%,end
What is this?

572
00:35:24.917 --> 00:35:27.875 line:95%,end
It's Ultron attempting to slow us down
while he makes his escape.

573
00:35:33.125 --> 00:35:34.500 line:95%,end
Okay, Vee,

574
00:35:34.583 --> 00:35:38.000 line:95%,end
you remember my seven-part lecture
on heroic landings?

575
00:35:45.917 --> 00:35:46.958 line:95%,end
Ultron!

576
00:35:53.083 --> 00:35:54.083 line:95%,end
What is this?

577
00:35:54.167 --> 00:35:58.167 line:95%,end
You once told me that hats
imply a journey about to begin.

578
00:35:59.458 --> 00:36:01.417 line:95%,end
Well, all journeys begin with hope.

579
00:36:02.625 --> 00:36:03.625 line:95%,end
And hope

580
00:36:04.917 --> 00:36:07.625 line:95%,end
is the only weapon
that's ever really worked for me.

581
00:36:09.167 --> 00:36:10.833 line:95%,end
You've chosen your son.

582
00:36:10.917 --> 00:36:12.292 line:95%,end
He's not my son.

583
00:36:14.125 --> 00:36:15.792 line:95%,end
But I can still save Thomas.

584
00:36:16.708 --> 00:36:18.833 line:95%,end
The only person who can save you now

585
00:36:19.792 --> 00:36:20.792 line:95%,end
is yourself.

586
00:36:29.750 --> 00:36:31.083 line:95%,end
Then this is goodbye.

587
00:36:32.125 --> 00:36:33.125 line:95%,end
Not goodbye.

588
00:36:34.083 --> 00:36:35.208 line:95%,end
You should know this.

589
00:36:35.875 --> 00:36:38.375 line:95%,end
Whatever you choose, whatever she chooses,

590
00:36:39.375 --> 00:36:41.042 line:95%,end
I will be coming for you both.

591
00:36:47.667 --> 00:36:49.875 line:95%,end
I'd be disappointed if you didn't.

592
00:37:15.958 --> 00:37:18.208 line:95%,end
Oh, my God, no! No, no, no, no, no!

593
00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:21.083 line:95%,end
-Friday, Friday. Friday.
-But you--

594
00:37:21.167 --> 00:37:23.500 line:95%,end
-You didn't even try and stop him.
-I promise you,

595
00:37:23.583 --> 00:37:26.625 line:95%,end
we will find them
and we will stop them both together.

596
00:37:30.125 --> 00:37:31.167 line:95%,end
No.

597
00:37:32.500 --> 00:37:33.583 line:95%,end
Not together.

598
00:37:37.250 --> 00:37:38.500 line:95%,end
Friday!

599
00:37:41.292 --> 00:37:42.333 line:95%,end
Friday!

600
00:37:46.250 --> 00:37:47.375 line:95%,end
No.

601
00:37:49.792 --> 00:37:51.500 line:95%,end
He broke the connection.

602
00:37:53.167 --> 00:37:56.708 line:95%,end
We can go after them, though, right?
We can run a trace.

603
00:37:56.792 --> 00:37:58.500 line:95%,end
The address is encrypted.

604
00:37:58.583 --> 00:37:59.875 line:95%,end
So, we hack it!

605
00:37:59.958 --> 00:38:02.250 line:95%,end
-There has to be a way. There--
-Edith.

606
00:38:03.375 --> 00:38:04.375 line:95%,end
She's gone.

607
00:38:06.833 --> 00:38:08.250 line:95%,end
But they'll delete her.

608
00:38:11.083 --> 00:38:13.542 line:95%,end
No, I can't process. I need-- [glitches]

609
00:38:14.333 --> 00:38:15.542 line:95%,end
It's Friday.

610
00:38:15.625 --> 00:38:17.792 line:95%,end
Please, Vision, I n--

611
00:38:19.667 --> 00:38:21.250 line:95%,end
I think I need defragging.

612
00:38:25.417 --> 00:38:26.958 line:95%,end
[sobbing]

613
00:38:32.250 --> 00:38:33.625 line:95%,end
You all right?

614
00:38:45.583 --> 00:38:46.583 line:95%,end
It's time.

615
00:38:47.417 --> 00:38:48.417 line:95%,end
For what?

616
00:38:50.208 --> 00:38:51.375 line:95%,end
To wake up.

617
00:39:24.625 --> 00:39:26.375 line:95%,end
Edith, what's our current location?

618
00:39:27.500 --> 00:39:29.750 line:95%,end
Where Ultron left your body
in the real world?

619
00:39:29.833 --> 00:39:32.708 line:95%,end
-Right, but where exactly is that?
-Um...

620
00:39:34.917 --> 00:39:36.667 line:95%,end
[animal growling]

621
00:39:38.042 --> 00:39:39.250 line:95%,end
-[gasps]
-[Vision] Oh.

622
00:39:42.500 --> 00:39:44.542 line:95%,end
Don't really know what I was expecting.

623
00:39:45.292 --> 00:39:48.125 line:95%,end
Well, it would appear that
Ultron has left us on some sort of

624
00:39:48.208 --> 00:39:50.458 line:95%,end
animal transport plane.

625
00:39:50.542 --> 00:39:52.208 line:95%,end
But on our way to where?

626
00:39:52.292 --> 00:39:53.500 line:95%,end
[U] "Poo."

627
00:40:01.833 --> 00:40:03.375 line:5%,start
We're on our way to Madripoor.

628
00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:11.958 line:95%,end
It would appear that Ultron has left us

629
00:40:12.042 --> 00:40:14.458 line:95%,end
on the way to Madripoor to rescue Thomas.

630
00:40:17.458 --> 00:40:18.708 line:95%,end
[Lisa] All right, listen, mate.

631
00:40:19.833 --> 00:40:20.958 line:95%,end
Lisa.

632
00:40:21.667 --> 00:40:25.583 line:95%,end
In the space of a single evening,
I've seen you fight robots, glitch out,

633
00:40:25.667 --> 00:40:28.083 line:95%,end
vaporize a billionaire, kidnap my mate,

634
00:40:28.167 --> 00:40:30.875 line:95%,end
and then clop like a zombie
onto this here cargo plane.

635
00:40:30.958 --> 00:40:32.292 line:95%,end
That's fine.

636
00:40:33.208 --> 00:40:35.375 line:95%,end
All I care about is...

637
00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:39.125 line:95%,end
Thomas.

638
00:40:43.042 --> 00:40:44.125 line:95%,end
Me too.

639
00:40:48.042 --> 00:40:49.500 line:95%,end
Let's bring him home.

640
00:41:05.958 --> 00:41:07.833 line:95%,end
[♪ closing theme music playing]
